<main id="main"><div class="shell"><section class="section">
  <h1 class="section__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <div class="panel"><p style="margin:0"><strong>This is a local demonstration.</strong>
    Anything typed into these forms is written to a SQLite file on this machine and nowhere
    else. No analytics, no cookies for tracking, no third-party requests, no network calls
    off this host.</p></div>
    <h3>What this demonstration stores</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The values submitted through the local forms, in <code>replica/database/replica.sqlite</code>.</li>
      <li>An append-only audit entry per submission, as the ERP scope requires.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>What you should not do</h3>
    <p>Do not enter anyone&rsquo;s real personal data into this demonstration. It has no access
    control, no encryption at rest, and no retention policy. Use obviously synthetic values.</p>
    <h3>The original portal&rsquo;s policy</h3>
    <p>The original publishes its own privacy policy. This replica does not reproduce its text
    and does not speak for it.</p>
  </div>
</section></div></main>
